'''Diego Navarro''' (7 September 1940{{Spaced en dash}}13 July 2020) was a [[Balisca|Baliscan]] politician and farmer, who served as the xth [[Secretary General of Balisca]] from 1983 to 1992. During his political career, Navarro was a member of the [[Ecological Action|Ecologist]] platform, representing the [[Baixa Arcàdia (commune district)|Baixa Arcàdia]] [[commune district]]. Navarro later became heavily involved in the development and implementation of the [[Low Impact Initiative|confederal response]] to the [[Special Period]] under [[Otávia Brito]]. He went on to win the [[1982 Baliscan premiership election|1982 premiership election]], succeeding Brito.

Navarro was notable for his [[W:Simple living|austere lifestyle]] and his donation of around 90 percent of his $2,500 monthly salary to charities related to carrying out [[W:Mutual aid|mutual aid]] in [[Rural society in Balisca|rural areas]]. 

